                <h3><b>Resource Allocation and Product Prioritization</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Resource allocation should directly support product priorities.
                    Instead of distributing resources equally across every initiative,
                    organizations should focus available capacity on projects and
                    capabilities that contribute the greatest strategic value.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Evaluate initiatives based on customer value and business impact.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Match specialized skills with initiatives that require them most.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Balance short-term delivery requirements with long-term product investments.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Reserve capacity for maintenance, technical improvements, and unexpected requirements.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Reassess allocation when product priorities or delivery conditions change.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
