<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Capacity Planning and Team Coordination</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Effective capacity planning provides visibility into how much work
                    product teams can realistically complete within a given period.
                    Understanding capacity helps product leaders create achievable
                    commitments and avoid excessive workload.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Capacity Assessment</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Review team availability, existing responsibilities, planned
                    initiatives, holidays, dependencies, and other commitments to
                    determine realistic delivery capacity.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Workload Balancing</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Monitor workloads across teams and individuals to identify areas where
                    additional support or redistribution may be required.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Cross-Functional Coordination</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Product delivery often depends on multiple teams. Coordinating
                    engineering, design, QA, product management, marketing, and operations
                    ensures that resources are available when needed.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Future Capacity Planning</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Anticipate future product requirements and identify upcoming hiring,
                    training, technology, or outsourcing needs before capacity becomes a
                    delivery constraint.
                </p>
            </div>

